## Format

- **MyST Markdown** (`.md`). Prefer ` ```{math} ` with optional `:label:` for
  numbered equations; inline `:math:` roles and `:eq:` cross-refs are fine.
- Citations: see `.cursor/rules/docs-cross-links.mdc` (canonical bib
  `docs/references.md`, `{ref}`Key <key>``). Cite foundational definitions,
  named propositions/algorithms, and special-function identities; add new
  `(key)=` entries when introducing a source.
- `index.md` maintains the toctree, grouped by topic (Distributions / Fitting /
  Portfolio & risk).

## Selective enrichment (not a full merge)

Tutorials stay executable demos.
Fitting and portfolio theory pages stay derivations.
For a high-overlap pair, put the key formula in the tutorial intro.
On `gig.md`, `gh.md`, and `varentropy.md`, link the derivation to xshi-math.
Do not paste code cells into a theory page.
Do not merge a tutorial and a theory page.

## When to Update

- Add a theory file for a new distribution or algorithm.
- For `gig.md`, `gh.md`, or `varentropy.md`, update the contract on that page.
- Link a moved derivation to the matching xshi-math page.
- Fix an error in place on any other theory page.
- Leave `em_algorithm.md` and `online_em.md` unchanged until batch B12.
- Add a cross-link both ways when a tutorial covers a theory-only topic.

## Relationship to Other Docs

- `docs/theory/` holds the GIG, GH, and varentropy contracts, plus derivations for the other topics.
- `dev-notes/tech_notes/` = **implementation notes**
- `docs/design/` = **design rationale**

## Gotchas

- Do not put a numerical floor or a solver tolerance on a theory page.
- On `gig.md`, `gh.md`, and `varentropy.md`, state the formula the code evaluates.
- Name a public method only when it evaluates that formula.
- On every other theory page, keep the derivation and omit the implementation.
- **Don't mix `.rst` and `.md`** — all theory content is MyST `.md`.
- **Don't leave named math bare.** "Hankel asymptotic", "Olver expansion",
  "MCECM", Hellinger propositions, etc. need `{ref}` (and DLMF section URLs
  where applicable). Prefer the primary source; use Shi2016 when the
  derivation lives there.
- A one-shot converter lives at `scripts/rst_theory_to_myst.py` (historical;
  theory is already MyST).
